---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import fedData from '../data/fedData.json';

const webAppSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebApplication",
  "name": "Net Worth Calculator by Age",
  "url": "https://getnetworthcalculator.com",
  "description": "Calculate your exact net worth percentile by age benchmarked against official US Federal Reserve Survey of Consumer Finances (SCF) data.",
  "applicationCategory": "FinanceApplication",
  "operatingSystem": "All",
  "offers": {
    "@type": "Offer",
    "price": "0",
    "priceCurrency": "USD"
  }
};

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the average net worth by age in the US?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "According to the US Federal Reserve Survey of Consumer Finances (SCF), median household net worth varies significantly by age: Under 35 is ~$39,000; 35-44 is ~$135,600; 45-54 is ~$247,200; 55-64 is ~$364,500; and 65-74 is ~$409,900."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How does the household net worth calculator work?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The household net worth calculator takes your total assets (savings, 401k, home equity, investments) minus liabilities (mortgages, student loans, credit cards) and maps your financial position against official Federal Reserve SCF population benchmarks."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What net worth makes you top 10% by age 30?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "For Americans under age 35, a household net worth of approximately $340,000 puts you in the top 10th percentile according to Federal Reserve data."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is a good benchmark net worth in San Francisco and HCOL cities?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "In San Francisco and the Bay Area, median net worth is ~$1.7 million to $2.2 million, and a net worth of $4.7 million+ is considered wealthy due to high real estate and tech equity values."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Should I include primary residence home equity in my net worth?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Total net worth includes home equity (home value minus mortgage balance). However, liquid net worth excludes primary residence home equity to focus on cash, investments, and retirement accounts. Our calculator includes a toggle so you can test both."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---

<Layout title="Net Worth Calculator by Age | US Wealth Percentiles" description="Calculate your exact net worth percentile by age benchmarked against official US Federal Reserve data. 100% free, private & anonymous.">
	
	<!-- JSON-LD Schema Scripts -->
	<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(webAppSchema)} />
	<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

	<main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-10 md:py-16">
		<header class="text-center mb-12 space-y-4">
			<div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3.5 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/30 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 text-xs font-semibold">
				<span>🇺🇸</span>
				<span>Official US Federal Reserve SCF Wealth Data (2026)</span>
			</div>
			
			<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
				Net Worth Calculator <span class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 font-normal">by Age (USA)</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="text-slate-850 dark:text-slate-400 text-base md:text-lg max-w-xl mx-auto font-normal leading-relaxed">
				Calculate your exact net worth percentile in America benchmarked against official US Federal Reserve population data.
			</p>
		</header>

		<!-- Quick Reference Snippet Box -->
		<div class="bg-emerald-950/20 border border-emerald-500/30 rounded-2xl p-5 md:p-6 mb-8 text-left space-y-2">
			<div class="text-[11px] font-extrabold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">⚡ Federal Reserve Net Worth Benchmarks by Age (2026)</div>
			<div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3 text-xs text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 font-semibold pt-1">
				<div>Under 35: <span class="text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-extrabold">$39,000</span></div>
				<div>35–44: <span class="text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-extrabold">$135,600</span></div>
				<div>45–54: <span class="text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-extrabold">$247,200</span></div>
				<div>55–64: <span class="text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-extrabold">$364,500</span></div>
			</div>
		</div>

		<!-- Main Interactive Calculator Panel -->
		<div class="p-6 md:p-10 rounded-3xl border border-slate-250 dark:border-slate-800/80 shadow-xl dark:shadow-2xl relative overflow-hidden backdrop-blur-xl bg-white/95 dark:bg-slate-900/40 transition-colors duration-300">
			
			<div class="space-y-8">
				<!-- Top Controls Bar: Currency Selector & Options -->
				<div class="flex items-center justify-between flex-wrap gap-4 pb-4 border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800/80">
					<div class="flex items-center gap-2">
						<label for="currency-select" class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-750 dark:text-slate-300">Currency (USD):</label>
						<select id="currency-select" class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-950 border border-slate-300 dark:border-slate-800 text-slate-900 dark:text-white text-xs font-bold rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 outline-none focus:ring-1 focus:ring-emerald-500 cursor-pointer">
							<option value="USD" data-symbol="$">USD ($) — US Fed Data</option>
						</select>
					</div>

					<!-- Option Toggle: Home Equity -->
					<div class="flex items-center gap-3">
						<label for="home-equity-toggle" class="text-xs font-bold text-slate-750 dark:text-slate-300 cursor-pointer">Include Home Equity</label>
						<label for="home-equity-toggle" class="relative inline-flex items-center cursor-pointer">
							<input type="checkbox" id="home-equity-toggle" checked class="sr-only peer" aria-label="Include Home Equity">
							<div class="w-9 h-5 bg-slate-300 dark:bg-slate-800 peer-focus:outline-none rounded-full peer peer-checked:after:translate-x-full peer-checked:after:border-white after:content-[''] after:absolute after:top-[2px] after:left-[2px] after:bg-white after:border-slate-300 after:border after:rounded-full after:h-4 after:w-4 after:transition-all peer-checked:bg-emerald-600"></div>
						</label>
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- Input 1: Age Slider -->
				<div class="space-y-3">
					<div class="flex justify-between items-center">
						<label id="age-label-id" for="age-input" class="text-base font-bold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
							Your Age
						</label>
						<span id="age-display" class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-950 px-4 py-1.5 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
							32 years
						</span>
					</div>
					<input type="range" id="age-input" min="18" max="80" value="32" class="w-full h-2 bg-slate-200 dark:bg-slate-950 rounded-lg appearance-none cursor-pointer accent-emerald-700 dark:accent-emerald-500 border border-slate-300 dark:border-slate-800" aria-label="Your Age" title="Your Age">
					<div class="flex justify-between text-xs text-slate-750 dark:text-slate-400 font-bold px-1">
						<span>18</span>
						<span>30</span>
						<span>40</span>
						<span>50</span>
						<span>60</span>
						<span>70</span>
						<span>80</span>
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- Input 2: Net Worth Input & Slider -->
				<div class="space-y-3">
					<div class="flex justify-between items-center flex-wrap gap-3">
						<label id="nw-label-id" for="nw-number-input" class="text-base font-bold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
							Total Net Worth (<span class="curr-symbol">$</span>)
						</label>
						<div class="relative">
							<span class="curr-symbol absolute left-3.5 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 text-slate-750 dark:text-slate-405 font-bold">$</span>
							<input type="number" id="nw-number-input" value="120000" step="5000" class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-950 border border-slate-300 dark:border-slate-800 text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 text-lg font-bold rounded-xl pl-8 pr-4 py-2.5 w-48 focus:ring-1 focus:ring-emerald-500 outline-none" aria-label="Total Net Worth">
						</div>
					</div>
					<label for="nw-slider-input" class="sr-only">Total Net Worth</label>
					<input type="range" id="nw-slider-input" min="-20000" max="2000000" step="5000" value="120000" class="w-full h-2 bg-slate-200 dark:bg-slate-950 rounded-lg appearance-none cursor-pointer accent-emerald-700 dark:accent-emerald-500 border border-slate-300 dark:border-slate-800" aria-label="Total Net Worth" title="Total Net Worth">
					<div class="flex justify-between text-xs text-slate-750 dark:text-slate-400 font-bold px-1">
						<span>-<span class="curr-symbol">$</span>20k</span>
						<span><span class="curr-symbol">$</span>100k</span>
						<span><span class="curr-symbol">$</span>500k</span>
						<span><span class="curr-symbol">$</span>1M</span>
						<span><span class="curr-symbol">$</span>2M+</span>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Dynamic Percentile Results Display -->
			<div class="mt-10 pt-8 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800/80 space-y-6">
				<div class="text-center space-y-2">
					<span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-755 dark:text-slate-400">Wealth Percentile Benchmark</span>
					<div id="percentile-badge" class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
						Top 28% Percentile
					</div>
					<p id="comparison-summary" class="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-300 text-base max-w-lg mx-auto font-normal">
						At age <span class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white font-semibold">32</span> with <span class="text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 font-semibold"><span class="curr-symbol">$</span>120,000</span> net worth, you have more wealth than <span class="text-emerald-750 dark:text-emerald-400 font-semibold">72%</span> of Americans in your age group.
					</p>
				</div>

				<!-- Interactive Visual Wealth Bell Curve SVG -->
				<div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-slate-100/70 dark:bg-slate-950/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800/80 space-y-2">
					<div class="flex justify-between text-xs font-bold text-slate-755 dark:text-slate-400">
						<span>US Population Wealth Distribution Curve</span>
						<span id="curve-marker-text" class="text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 font-bold">You are at 72%</span>
					</div>
					<div class="relative w-full h-24">
						<svg class="w-full h-full overflow-visible" viewBox="0 0 400 80" preserveAspectRatio="none" role="img" aria-label="Interactive Wealth Distribution Curve Chart">
							<!-- Bell Curve Path -->
							<path d="M 0,75 Q 100,75 160,55 T 200,10 T 240,55 Q 300,75 400,75" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" class="text-slate-450 dark:text-slate-800" stroke-width="3"/>
							<!-- Shaded Area Under Curve -->
							<path id="curve-fill-path" d="M 0,75 Q 100,75 160,55 T 200,10 T 240,55 Q 300,75 400,75 L 400,80 L 0,80 Z" class="fill-emerald-500/20"/>
							<!-- Active Dot Marker -->
							<circle id="curve-dot" cx="288" cy="62" r="7" class="fill-emerald-600 stroke-white dark:stroke-slate-950" stroke-width="2.5"/>
						</svg>
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- Benchmarks Matrix Grid -->
				<div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3 pt-2">
					<div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-100/80 dark:bg-slate-950/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800/80 text-center">
						<span class="text-xs text-slate-755 dark:text-slate-400 block mb-1 font-bold">Median (50th)</span>
						<span id="bm-p50" class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">$39,000</span>
					</div>
					<div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-100/80 dark:bg-slate-950/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800/80 text-center">
						<span class="text-xs text-slate-755 dark:text-slate-400 block mb-1 font-bold">Top 25% (75th)</span>
						<span id="bm-p75" class="text-base font-bold text-slate-750 dark:text-slate-200">$145,000</span>
					</div>
					<div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-100/80 dark:bg-slate-950/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800/80 text-center">
						<span class="text-xs text-slate-755 dark:text-slate-400 block mb-1 font-bold">Top 10% (90th)</span>
						<span id="bm-p90" class="text-base font-bold text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400">$340,000</span>
					</div>
					<div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-100/80 dark:bg-slate-950/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800/80 text-center">
						<span class="text-xs text-slate-755 dark:text-slate-400 block mb-1 font-bold">Top 1% (99th)</span>
						<span id="bm-p99" class="text-base font-bold text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400">$1,400,000</span>
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- Age-Based Ideal Asset Allocation Benchmark Card -->
				<div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-slate-100/90 dark:bg-slate-950 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800/80 space-y-3">
					<div class="flex items-center justify-between">
						<span class="text-xs font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white uppercase tracking-wider">Recommended Asset Allocation for Age <span id="asset-age-label">32</span></span>
						<span class="text-xs text-slate-755 dark:text-slate-400 font-bold">Benchmark Model</span>
					</div>
					<div id="asset-breakdown-grid" class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-2 text-xs">
						<!-- Populated via JS -->
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- Actionable Target Box & Viral Share Buttons -->
				<div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-slate-950 border border-emerald-200 dark:border-slate-800 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4 text-center sm:text-left">
					<div>
						<span class="text-xs font-bold text-emerald-855 dark:text-emerald-450 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1">Wealth Goal Milestone</span>
						<p id="milestone-text" class="text-sm text-slate-855 dark:text-slate-300">
							To reach the <strong class="text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-450">Top 10%</strong> for your age group, you need an additional <strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white">$220,000</strong>.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="flex items-center gap-2 shrink-0">
						<button id="copy-summary-btn" class="px-3.5 py-2.5 rounded-xl bg-emerald-700 hover:bg-emerald-600 text-white font-bold text-xs flex items-center gap-1.5 transition-all shadow-sm">
							<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
								<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 16H6a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h8a2 2 0 002-2v2m-6 12h8a2 2 0 002-2v-8a2 2 0 00-2-2h-8a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z" />
							</svg>
							<span>Copy Card</span>
						</button>
						<button id="share-twitter-btn" class="px-3 py-2.5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 dark:bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-800 text-white font-bold text-xs flex items-center gap-1.5 transition-all shadow-sm">
							<span>𝕏 Share</span>
						</button>
						<button id="share-wa-btn" class="px-3 py-2.5 rounded-xl bg-emerald-600 hover:bg-emerald-500 text-white font-bold text-xs flex items-center gap-1.5 transition-all shadow-sm">
							<span>💬 WhatsApp</span>
						</button>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>

		<!-- AI Overview & Featured Snippet Callout Box -->
		<section class="mt-12 p-6 md:p-8 rounded-3xl bg-emerald-500/10 dark:bg-emerald-950/30 border border-emerald-500/30 space-y-3">
			<div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 uppercase tracking-wider">
				<span>⚡</span> <span>Quick Answer: US Net Worth Benchmarks by Age (2026)</span>
			</div>
			<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">What is the Average Net Worth by Age in America?</h2>
			<p class="text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
				According to the latest Federal Reserve Survey of Consumer Finances (SCF), median household net worth in the US is: <strong>Under 35 ($39,000)</strong>, <strong>35–44 ($135,600)</strong>, <strong>45–54 ($247,200)</strong>, <strong>55–64 ($364,500)</strong>, and <strong>65–74 ($409,900)</strong>. Median net worth represents the exact 50th percentile midpoint, eliminating billionaire distortion caused by mean average figures.
			</p>
		</section>

		<!-- Federal Reserve Data Methodology & Privacy Trust Card -->
		<section class="mt-16 p-6 md:p-8 rounded-3xl bg-slate-100/80 dark:bg-slate-950/70 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800/80 space-y-4">
			<div class="flex items-center gap-3">
				<div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-emerald-500/10 dark:bg-emerald-500/20 border border-emerald-500/30 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">
					<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
						<path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z" />
					</svg>
				</div>
				<div>
					<h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Federal Reserve SCF Data Governance & Privacy Guarantee</h3>
					<p class="text-xs text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-400">Official United States Population Benchmark Methodology</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 pt-2 text-xs text-slate-750 dark:text-slate-300">
				<div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800/80 space-y-1">
					<strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white block font-bold">1. Primary Source Dataset</strong>
					<p class="leading-relaxed">Derived directly from the Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System's triennial Survey of Consumer Finances (SCF), covering comprehensive US household asset distributions.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800/80 space-y-1">
					<strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white block font-bold">2. Median Percentile Math</strong>
					<p class="leading-relaxed">Calculated using median distributions per age cohort (Under 35, 35–44, 45–54, 55–64, 65–74, 75+) rather than mean averages to eliminate billionaire distortion.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800/80 space-y-1">
					<strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white block font-bold">3. 100% Client-Side Privacy</strong>
					<p class="leading-relaxed">All calculations execute directly inside your browser. No financial data, age inputs, or net worth values are stored, logged, or sent to any server.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- 1,800+ Word On-Page Financial Masterclass Guide Section -->
		<article class="mt-16 max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-10 text-slate-755 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed font-normal border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 pt-12">
			<section class="space-y-4">
				<h2 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">The Complete Guide to Net Worth Benchmarking by Age</h2>
				<p>
					Net worth is the single most comprehensive metric for measuring personal financial health. Unlike annual income—which measures incoming cash flow over a 12-month period—net worth measures accumulated financial security: your total assets minus your total liabilities.
				</p>
				<p>
					According to official data from the <strong>Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System (Survey of Consumer Finances)</strong>, household net worth varies dramatically based on age, education level, housing tenure, and career longevity. Benchmarking your financial position against age-specific percentiles provides essential clarity for retirement planning, debt payoff scheduling, and investment asset allocation.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="space-y-4">
				<h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Why Median Net Worth Outperforms Average (Mean) Benchmarks</h3>
				<p>
					When evaluating financial benchmark reports, it is critical to distinguish between <strong>Median Net Worth</strong> and <strong>Average Net Worth</strong>.
				</p>
				<div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-slate-100/90 dark:bg-slate-950 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 space-y-3 my-4">
					<p><strong>• Median Net Worth (50th Percentile):</strong> Represents the exact middle American household. Exactly 50% of households have a higher net worth, and 50% have lower. For Americans aged 35–44, the median net worth is <strong>$135,600</strong>.</p>
					<p><strong>• Average Net Worth (Mean):</strong> Calculated by adding all net worth values and dividing by the total number of households. This figure is heavily distorted upward by multi-billionaires like Elon Musk and Jeff Bezos. For Americans aged 35–44, the average net worth is <strong>$549,000</strong>—more than 4x the median figure!</p>
				</div>
				<p>
					For realistic financial goal-setting, <strong>median percentile rankings</strong> provide a far more accurate reflection of actual household wealth distribution.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="space-y-4">
				<h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Net Worth Milestones Across Life Stages</h3>
				<div class="space-y-4">
					<div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800/80 bg-white/95 dark:bg-slate-900/40">
						<h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white text-base mb-1">Under Age 35: Building Foundation (Median: $39,000 | Top 10%: $340,000)</h4>
						<p class="text-xs text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-400">Young professionals focus on eliminating high-interest student loans, accumulating emergency savings (3–6 months), and initiating 401(k) or Roth IRA contributions to capture employer matching funds.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800/80 bg-white/95 dark:bg-slate-900/40">
						<h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white text-base mb-1">Ages 35–44: Home Equity & Asset Compound Stage (Median: $135,600 | Top 10%: $980,000)</h4>
						<p class="text-xs text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-400">Peak career advancement years where home equity begins compounding alongside tax-advantaged retirement accounts (401k, HSA, Roth IRA). Many target reaching 1x to 3x their annual salary in net worth by age 40.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800/80 bg-white/95 dark:bg-slate-900/40">
